clock nothing 00000000 a move
clock answers 00000000 a wide add's high word
clock answers 00000000 doubled

# writings the system answers alike: an operation written where the ruleset holds the other, each
# giving the same machine code. A reading in one is the ruleset's form in the other.

# the fields of an instruction a question on the run channel turns, each its first bit and its bits, a
# barrier holding every bit setting none; then the container the system accepted, which every such
# question is put in: the kernel it enters at, then its bytes in hex, sixty-four a row. A question's code,
# registers and exits replace the code's.
field stall 105 4
field write_barrier 110 3
container kernel interface_ask
